{
 "cards": [
  {
   "dot": "emerald",
   "items": [
    "The record database stays the single leader; every derived copy follows its order",
    "Business row and outbox row commit in one transaction, so neither exists without the other",
    "CDC reads the stable outbox contract, never the internal domain tables"
   ],
   "title": "One leader"
  },
  {
   "dot": "cyan",
   "items": [
    "The outbox event topic is append-only and keyed by event id for dedup, with retention",
    "The entity-state topic is compacted and keyed by entity key; deletes arrive as tombstones",
    "The record snapshot is a one-off bulk seed at LSN B and is discarded after catch-up"
   ],
   "title": "Three contracts"
  },
  {
   "dot": "amber",
   "items": [
    "The snapshot reads from a replica at a bounded rate, so production barely notices",
    "Streaming starts at LSN B with event-ID dedup absorbing the snapshot overlap",
    "A kill mid-bootstrap resumes from the checkpoint; the checksum at the boundary proves it"
   ],
   "title": "Throttled bootstrap"
  }
 ],
